-- title:
--   Charts at affine places not fixed by φ²
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ which is surjective, modular polynomial data `data` at $q$ (a monic bivariate integral polynomial $\Phi$ of degree $\psi(q)$ killing the pair $(j, j_q)$ of $q$-expansions) satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, i.e. the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(Y^q - X)(Y - X^q)$, together with integrality hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` for the two degeneracy embeddings `heckeAlphaBar`, `heckeBetaBar` of the level-$N$ into the level-$Nq$ geometric function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data, $R$ a prolongation tuple over $P$, and `fm` a fibre model for $N$, $A$, $q$, $k$, $\mathrm{red}$. Assume further: modular polynomial data `dataAll` for every divisor $d \mid N$, separability `hsep` of the level-$N$ polynomial after reduction to $k$ and passage to $k(X)$, the identification `hP` of $P.\mathrm{sp}$ with the specialisation map `fm.spPlace` attached to `fm`, $q \nmid N$, and `hBFC`: every element of the level-$N$ geometric field which is integral over the subring generated by the constants from $A$ and $\bar j$ lies in `fm.BFin`. The conclusion is that for every place $v$ of $k(j, j_N) =$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N` with `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel` applied twice to $v$ different from $v$ (this operator restricts $v$ along the $q$-power expansion map and transports it back) and with $v$ affine, meaning that both $j$ and $j_N$ lie in the valuation subring of $v$, there is a set $S$ of level-$Nq$ functions which is a chart at $v$ for $R$ in the sense of `IsChartAt`: its elements are $R_1$-integral with residues regular at $v$; it contains the images under `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` of $\bar j$ and $\bar j_N$ at affine $v$ (and of their inverses at non-affine $v$) and all constants from $A$; it satisfies the division law for level-$N$ functions regular above $v$, the value law at the places of the first kind over $v$, separation of the places of the second kind, the étale condition `ChartEtaleAt`, the dichotomy that every place reducing to $v$ is strict of the first or second kind, and regularity of its elements at every place over $v$.
--
--   This provides the local charts on the level-$Nq$ curve over the ordinary, non-fixed affine points of the level-$N$ fibre at $q$, in the picture of the special fibre of $X_0(Nq)$ at $q$ as two copies of $X_0(N)$ meeting at the supersingular points. It is used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.hasCharts_of_sp_eq_spPlace_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.hasCharts_of_sp_eq_spPlace_of_not_dvd), which assembles charts at all places.
